WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.195 --> 00:00:02.470
Your first loss doesn’t end your tournament.

2
00:00:02.515 --> 00:00:04.050
In Lobo’s Top 40,

3
00:00:04.115 --> 00:00:06.370
you still have a route to the championship.

4
00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:07.955
Here’s how the bracket works,

5
00:00:07.955 --> 00:00:09.610
how to prepare for each match,

6
00:00:09.715 --> 00:00:11.770
and what to do when your game is finished.

7
00:00:12.015 --> 00:00:14.090
The tournament has twenty-five players,

8
00:00:14.135 --> 00:00:16.635
with every game played at three hundred points.

9
00:00:16.635 --> 00:00:20.075
Registration is closed, and the seeded bracket is published on

10
00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:21.850
the Lobo Infinity Portal.

11
00:00:22.435 --> 00:00:24.930
Seeding uses Infinity the Meta ratings,

12
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:27.690
with Commissioner placements for unrated players.

13
00:00:27.715 --> 00:00:30.570
The bracket has thirty-two starting positions,

14
00:00:30.835 --> 00:00:35.110
so the seven highest seeds receive an opening-round bye.

15
00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:37.710
That leaves nine opening matches.

16
00:00:37.835 --> 00:00:40.250
A bye advances you automatically;

17
00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:43.550
it isn’t a game you need to arrange or report.

18
00:00:44.195 --> 00:00:46.570
Everyone begins in the Winners Bracket.

19
00:00:47.235 --> 00:00:49.710
Imagine you lose your opening game.

20
00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:52.035
You move into the Losers Bracket,

21
00:00:52.035 --> 00:00:53.710
but you’re still in the tournament.

22
00:00:53.935 --> 00:00:57.150
Win there, and you continue along that path.

23
00:00:57.535 --> 00:01:00.770
Lose again, and you’re eliminated.

24
00:01:00.895 --> 00:01:03.295
Your second match loss ends your run,

25
00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:04.770
wherever it happens.

26
00:01:05.175 --> 00:01:06.615
To find your next game,

27
00:01:06.615 --> 00:01:10.030
open the Top 40 event page and select Bracket.

28
00:01:10.535 --> 00:01:13.030
Check your opponent and your match’s status.

29
00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:16.270
Later opponents depend on earlier results,

30
00:01:16.535 --> 00:01:20.710
so wait until your matchup is confirmed and active before playing it.

31
00:01:21.315 --> 00:01:24.770
You can change your army and your army list between rounds.

32
00:01:24.835 --> 00:01:28.630
You’re not required to play the same army or list throughout the tournament.

33
00:01:29.315 --> 00:01:31.530
Choose what you want to bring for each game,

34
00:01:31.715 --> 00:01:34.550
keeping every list within the three-hundred-point limit.

35
00:01:34.635 --> 00:01:36.270
Before setting up the table,

36
00:01:36.355 --> 00:01:39.670
check the mission and map assigned to your bracket and round.

37
00:01:40.175 --> 00:01:42.010
Those two details matter:

38
00:01:42.415 --> 00:01:45.570
Winners and Losers rounds have their own assignments.

39
00:01:45.655 --> 00:01:48.550
The opening mission is Corporate Appropriation,

40
00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.750
played on Lobo Tourney Map One,

41
00:01:50.995 --> 00:01:52.910
Asterion Research Campus.

42
00:01:52.995 --> 00:01:56.355
The complete mission and map rotation is available on the event

43
00:01:56.355 --> 00:02:01.010
overview, with links to the assigned maps and Mission Geist rules.

44
00:02:01.395 --> 00:02:06.610
For Map One, the portal provides a saved-object download and a Windows installer.

45
00:02:06.695 --> 00:02:09.549
Load the map using the table’s map loader,

46
00:02:09.575 --> 00:02:13.570
then use its Deployment and Mission controls to check the setup.

47
00:02:13.755 --> 00:02:18.750
Confirm the terrain rules and objective positions with your opponent before starting.

48
00:02:18.815 --> 00:02:21.390
The planned opening is November first,

49
00:02:21.415 --> 00:02:25.750
twenty twenty-six, at nine a.m. Eastern.

50
00:02:26.135 --> 00:02:29.350
The Organizer releases the opening matches manually.

51
00:02:29.455 --> 00:02:31.410
Once your match becomes active,

52
00:02:31.555 --> 00:02:35.530
you receive at least seven full days to arrange and complete it.

53
00:02:35.875 --> 00:02:37.730
Contact your opponent promptly,

54
00:02:38.055 --> 00:02:39.290
agree on a time,

55
00:02:39.435 --> 00:02:42.150
and check the exact deadline shown on the portal.

56
00:02:42.215 --> 00:02:45.390
Later matches activate as the bracket progresses,

57
00:02:45.675 --> 00:02:49.110
so don’t assume everyone shares the same deadline.

58
00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.550
If scheduling becomes difficult,

59
00:02:51.775 --> 00:02:53.910
or your opponent isn’t responding,

60
00:02:54.055 --> 00:02:56.170
contact the Organizer early.

61
00:02:56.215 --> 00:02:59.830
Defaults, forfeits, missed deadlines,

62
00:02:59.895 --> 00:03:02.830
and scheduling disputes are handled by the Organizer.

63
00:03:03.295 --> 00:03:06.935
After your game, use Submit Game on the portal and choose

64
00:03:06.935 --> 00:03:08.750
Submit Top 40 Game.

65
00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:11.110
Select the correct players and mission,

66
00:03:11.235 --> 00:03:14.090
then enter both armies and army codes,

67
00:03:14.235 --> 00:03:15.650
who took first turn,

68
00:03:15.735 --> 00:03:18.910
the result, and both players’ Tournament Points,

69
00:03:18.975 --> 00:03:21.590
Objective Points, and Victory Points.

70
00:03:21.755 --> 00:03:25.450
Agree on those details with your opponent before submitting.

71
00:03:25.995 --> 00:03:28.330
Every bracket match needs a winner.

72
00:03:28.415 --> 00:03:30.150
If the game finishes drawn,

73
00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:32.330
Victory Points decide the winner.

74
00:03:32.415 --> 00:03:34.710
If Victory Points are also tied,

75
00:03:34.875 --> 00:03:37.250
contact the Organizer for a ruling.

76
00:03:37.815 --> 00:03:39.710
Once your result has been processed,

77
00:03:39.735 --> 00:03:41.895
check the bracket for your next matchup.

78
00:03:41.895 --> 00:03:47.690
The Grand Final brings together the Winners Bracket finalist and the Losers Bracket finalist.

79
00:03:48.235 --> 00:03:52.210
The unbeaten finalist needs one win to become champion.

80
00:03:52.355 --> 00:03:55.490
If the Losers finalist wins that first final,

81
00:03:55.655 --> 00:03:57.950
both players now have one loss,

82
00:03:58.075 --> 00:04:00.210
so they play a reset final.

83
00:04:00.435 --> 00:04:03.195
The winner of that second final takes the title.

84
00:04:03.195 --> 00:04:04.730
Before your first game,

85
00:04:04.875 --> 00:04:06.850
open the Top 40 event page,

86
00:04:07.015 --> 00:04:09.875
find your matchup, read your assigned mission,

87
00:04:09.875 --> 00:04:11.530
and contact your opponent.

88
00:04:11.735 --> 00:04:13.571
That’s where your tournament begins.
